ocal file system). So likely they mean: store on the server\\'s temp directory (so not filling up the /public folder) and still serve from there via a route that reads from temp.\\n\\nWe\\'ll implement a new API route for serving uploads when LOCAL_STORE true? But we can also just store in temp under a subfolder that is served as static? We could add that temp folder to static serving in next.config.js? That\\'s messy.\\n\\nGiven time, we\\'ll adjust storage to use LOCAL_STORE for storage root, and also adjust getUrl to return a path that is served via a new route: maybe `/api/local-upload/${key}`. However, we need to see if the frontend expects the storedPath to be a URL that can be used for playback (like video src). If we change the URL pattern, the frontend might break.\\n\\nLooking at init route: storedPath = StorageEngine.getUrl(storageKey); then storedPath is stored in DB as filePath. Later likely used to serve video. So we need to keep the URL pattern compatible with existing serving mechanism. Probably there is a route that serves files from /uploads/* (like from public/uploads). Let\\'s check if there is a route for serving uploads.\\n\\nSearch for route that handles uploads: maybe in app/api/upload/direct?route.ts.\\n\\nLet\\'s check.\\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9721c92bdf7579b2', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Glob', 'arguments': '{\"pattern\": \"src/app/api/upload/**/route.ts\"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9721c92bdf7579b2', 'content': 'src\\\\app\\\\api\\\\upload\\\\finalize\\\\route.ts\\nsrc\\\\app\\\\api\\\\upload\\\\init\\\\route.ts\\nsrc\\\\app\\\\api\\\\upload\\\\direct\\\\route.ts\\nsrc\\\\app\\\\api\\\\upload\\\\route.ts'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'reasoning_content': \"We need to look at the upload direct route which handles the actual file upload.\\nLet's read it.\\n\", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-907657ba3b902787', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Read', 'arguments': '{\"file_path\": \"D:\\\\\\\\Code\\\\\\\\yout\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\api\\\\\\\\upload\\\\\\\\direct\\\\\\\\route.ts\"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'chatcmpl-tool-907657ba3b902787', 'content': '1\\timport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\"\\n2\\timport { getServerSession } from \"next-auth\"\\n3\\timport { authOptions } from \"@/lib/auth\"\\n4\\timport { logger } from \"@/lib/logger\"\\n5\\timport fs from \"fs\"\\n6\\timport path from \"path\"\\n7\\timport { pipeline } from \"stream/promises\"\\n8\\timport { getStoragePath } from \"@/lib/storage-utils\"\\n9\\t\\n10\\t\\n11\\texport async function PUT(request: NextRequest) {\\n12\\t  try {\\n13\\t    const session = await getServerSession(authOptions)\\n14\\t    if (!session?.user?.id) {\\n15\\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Unauthorized\" }, { status: 401 })\\n16\\t    }\\n17\\t\\n18\\t    const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url)\\n19\\t    const key = searchParams.get(\"key\")\\n20\\t\\n21\\t    if (!key) {\\n22\\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Missing key\" }, { status: 400 })\\n23\\t    }\\n24\\t\\n25\\t    const localDest = getStoragePath(\"uploads\", key)\\n26\\t    const destDir = path.dirname(localDest)\\n27\\t    \\n28\\t    if (!fs.existsSync(destDir)) {\\n29\\t      fs.mkdirSync(destDir, { recursive: true })\\n30\\t    }\\n31\\t\\n32\\t    // Use pipeline for efficient streaming and backpressure handling\\n33\\t    const writeStream = fs.createWriteStream(localDest)\\n34\\t    \\n35\\t    if (!request.body) {\\n36\\t      throw new Error(\"No request body\")\\n37\\t    }\\n38\\t\\n39\\t    // Readable.fromWeb(request.body) is needed if request.body is a web stream\\n40\\t    // In Next.js App Router, request.body is already a ReadableStream (web stream)\\n41\\t    // We can pipe it directly in modern Node environments or use Readable.fromWeb\\n42\\t    await pipeline(request.body as any, writeStream)\\n43\\t\\n44\\t    logger.info(`Direct upload complete: ${key}`)\\n45\\t\\n46\\t    return NextResponse.json({\\n47\\t      success: true,\\n48\\t      path: `/uploads/${key}`\\n49\\t    })\\n50\\t  } catch (error) {\\n51\\t    logger.error(error, \"Direct upload failure\")\\n52\\t    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Upload failed\" }, { status: 500 })\\n53\\t  }\\n54\\t}\\n55\\t'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'reasoning_content': \"The user wants me to scan this folder and complete what remains to make a completely operational and real working system. They deployed it on Railway free with Redis too, and they mention upload/download not working. They want to upload to server /public or storage if configured, but should use system temp local storage if local_store env is true, otherwise server base config. They want a hybrid system, don't remove /public folder fallback or r2 storage if configured, just add env that tells local_store if true store on user own computer temp storage if not use server base config.\\n\\nI need to examine the codebase more, see what's missing, and fix the upload/download functionality. Let me look at more files, especially the upload-related routes and storage configuration.\\n\\nFirst, let me check if there's any .env.example or configuration files. Also check for Redis usage since they mentioned Redis.\\n\\nLet me look at the lib/db/index.ts to see database setup.\\n\", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b263fb7ab932d4ad', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Read', 'arguments': '{\"file_path\": \"D:\\\\\\\\Code\\\\\\\\yout\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\lib\\\\\\\\db\\\\\\\\index.ts\"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b263fb7ab932d4ad', 'content': '1\\timport { drizzle } from \"drizzle-orm/libsql\"\\n2\\timport { createClient } from \"@libsql/client\"\\n3\\timport * as schema from \"./schema\"\\n4\\t\\n5\\t// Create client\\n6\\tconst client = createClient({\\n7\\t  url: process.env.DATABASE_URL || \"file:./dev.db\",\\n8\\t  authToken: process.env.TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN,\\n9\\t})\\n10\\t\\n11\\t// Create DB instance\\n12\\texport const db = drizzle(client, { schema })\\n13\\t\\n14\\t// Export schema for convenience\\n15\\texport * from \"./schema\"\\n16\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nThe task tools haven\\'t been used recently. If you\\'re working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\\n\\n</system-reminder>'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'reasoning_content': 'We are in a project that is a video upload/download system. The user says:\\n - upload and download not working\\n - wants to deploy on Railway free and Redis too\\n - wants to upload videos to the server on /public or storage if configured, but if not configured, use system temp local storage (so server doesn\\'t take load) and run smooth without storage being needed (meaning: use local temp storage on the user\\'s computer? Actually, the user says: \"if configure it should use system temp local storage to store file so server doent take load and run this smooth and no staorage is neded and upload imedialty\"\\n\\nLet me interpret:\\n The user wants:\\n   - If local_store is enabled (via env), then store uploaded files in the system\\'s temporary directory (on the server? or on the user\\'s computer?).\\n   - But note: the server is running on Railway. The user says: \"system temp local storage\" meaning the server\\'s temporary directory? But then they say: \"so server doent take load\" - if we store on the server\\'s temp, then the server still uses disk.\\n\\n However, the user also says: \"no storage is neded\" and \"upload imedialty\". This is confusing.\\n\\n Let me re-read: \"keep in mind and its upload download not wokring and why is