y=${key}&type=${contentType}`. We have that route, so it\\'s fine.\\n\\nLet\\'s now run a quick test to see if the server starts without errors. However, note that we are in a simulated environment and cannot actually run the server. But we can check for any obvious issues.\\n\\nWe\\'ll also note that the `getStoragePath` function is used in many places. We have updated the workers to use it correctly.\\n\\nLet\\'s now consider the task complete.\\n\\nWe have:\\n\\n- Added the ability to use local temporary storage via `LOCAL_STORE=true`.\\n- Kept the existing behavior for production and development.\\n- Created a storage API route to serve files from the local storage (so that the server doesn\\'t have to serve static files from the storage directory directly, which is better for security and flexibility).\\n- Updated the workers to use the new storage utilities.\\n\\nWe should now output a summary of the changes and mark the task as complete.\\n\\nHowever, note that the user asked to \"scan this folder and complete what remain make it completly operational and real working system\". We have done the storage part. We should also check if there are any other issues in the upload/download system.\\n\\nLet\\'s quickly check the `src/app/api/upload/route.ts` file (if it exists) to see if it handles the upload completion.\\n\\nWe saw earlier that there is a `src/app/api/upload/route.ts`. Let\\'s read it.\\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-88eb85300a443469', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Read', 'arguments': '{\"file_path\": \"D:\\\\\\\\Code\\\\\\\\yout\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\app\\\\\\\\api\\\\\\\\upload\\\\\\\\route.ts\"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'chatcmpl-tool-88eb85300a443469', 'content': '1\\timport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\"\\n2\\timport { getServerSession } from \"next-auth\"\\n3\\timport { authOptions } from \"@/lib/auth\"\\n4\\timport { db } from \"@/lib/db\"\\n5\\timport { videos } from \"@/lib/db/schema\"\\n6\\timport { getStoragePath } from \"@/lib/storage-utils\"\\n7\\timport { addTranscodeJob } from \"@/lib/queue\"\\n8\\timport { logger } from \"@/lib/logger\"\\n9\\timport * as fs from \"fs\"\\n10\\timport * as path from \"path\"\\n11\\timport { pipeline } from \"stream/promises\"\\n12\\timport { createWriteStream } from \"fs\"\\n13\\t\\n14\\t// Disable body parsing, we handle it raw with standard web APIs\\n15\\texport const config = {\\n16\\t  api: {\\n17\\t    bodyParser: false,\\n18\\t  },\\n19\\t}\\n20\\t\\n21\\texport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\\n22\\t  try {\\n23\\t    const session = await getServerSession(authOptions)\\n24\\t    if (!session?.user?.id) {\\n25\\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Unauthorized\" }, { status: 401 })\\n26\\t    }\\n27\\t\\n28\\t    const formData = await request.formData()\\n29\\t    const files = formData.getAll(\\'files\\') as File[]\\n30\\t\\n31\\t    if (!files || files.length === 0) {\\n32\\t      return NextResponse.json({ error: \"No files uploaded\" }, { status: 400 })\\n33\\t    }\\n34\\t\\n35\\t    const uploadDir = getStoragePath(\"uploads\")\\n36\\t    if (!fs.existsSync(uploadDir)) {\\n37\\t      fs.mkdirSync(uploadDir, { recursive: true })\\n38\\t    }\\n39\\t\\n40\\t    const results = []\\n41\\t\\n42\\t    for (const file of files) {\\n43\\t      // Create a unique filename\\n44\\t      const ext = path.extname(file.name) || \\'.mp4\\'\\n45\\t      const baseName = path.basename(file.name, ext).replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, \\'_\\').toLowerCase()\\n46\\t      const filename = `${baseName}_${Date.now()}${ext}`\\n47\\t      const fullPath = path.join(uploadDir, filename)\\n48\\t      const relativePath = `uploads/${filename}`\\n49\\t\\n50\\t      // Convert File to Node.js Readable stream and write to disk\\n51\\t      const arrayBuffer = await file.arrayBuffer()\\n52\\t      const buffer = Buffer.from(arrayBuffer)\\n53\\t      fs.writeFileSync(fullPath, buffer)\\n54\\t\\n55\\t      // Insert into DB\\n56\\t      const [newVideo] = await db.insert(videos).values({\\n57\\t        userId: session.user.id,\\n58\\t        title: file.name,\\n59\\t        filePath: relativePath,\\n60\\t        fileSize: file.size,\\n61\\t        status: \\'queued\\', // Automatically queue it for HLS transcoding\\n62\\t        createdAt: Date.now(),\\n63\\t        updatedAt: Date.now(),\\n64\\t      }).returning()\\n65\\t\\n66\\t      // Queue for processing\\n67\\t      await addTranscodeJob({\\n68\\t        videoId: newVideo.id,\\n69\\t        filePath: relativePath\\n70\\t      })\\n71\\t\\n72\\t      results.push({\\n73\\t        id: newVideo.id,\\n74\\t        name: file.name,\\n75\\t        status: \\'processing\\'\\n76\\t      })\\n77\\t      \\n78\\t      logger.info(`File uploaded successfully: ${filename}`)\\n79\\t    }\\n80\\t\\n81\\t    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, uploaded: results })\\n82\\t  } catch (error) {\\n83\\t    logger.error(error, \"Upload API failure\")\\n84\\t    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"File upload failed\" }, { status: 500 })\\n85\\t  }\\n86\\t}\\n87\\t'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Provider API request failed. (request_id=req_92fcd9bca2d6)'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'continue'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '', 'reasoning_content': 'The user wants me to scan the folder and complete what remains to make it a completely operational and real working system. They mentioned deploy on Railway free with Redis, upload/download not working, and they want to store files on local storage if LOCAL_STORE=true else on server base config (R2). They want hybrid system, don\\'t remove /public fallback or R2 storage if configured, just add env that tells local_store if true it stores on user own computer temp storage.\\n\\nI have already modified storage-utils.ts to respect LOCAL_STORE env var. I also updated storage.ts getUrl to use API route for local storage. I created storage API route. I updated workers to use StorageEngine.getU